}
\details{
The package has four faces. The manifest itself (\link{orchestra_manifest}) is a
versioned, integrity-hashed, provenance-tracked \code{S7} record of one
inference. The consumer guard (\link{verify_manifest} and \link{consume_manifest})
turns silent schema drift and silent payload tampering into loud, early
failures. The provenance vocabulary (\link{grounding_token},
\link{combine_grounding}) propagates a worst-case grounding label so a verdict
resting on an unverified fact is labelled as such. The refusal contract
(\link{is_orchestra_refusal}, \link{is_orchestra_decline}) lets a gate recognise any
component's structured refusal or abstention without enumerating component
classes.
